# The Circle fills (0.16.20, issues #2 and #3): on the Progression page the first five black keys write a progression that moves round the
# circle of fifths, in the scale, saved with the piece like any: ii V I I, vi ii V I, iii vi ii V I I, I vi ii V, the whole circle
# I IV vii iii vi ii V I. Each chord takes the chosen slot's bars; the slots after the fill are emptied; Play goes to Loop. A pentatonic
# scale has no circle to walk: refused.
seed 0
wait 3000
press EDIT
wait 600
release EDIT
wait 100
expect view 5
expect pool 0x5AD
shot circle_page.png
# the chosen slot's bars (slot 1: 4 bars heard, one step up: 8) go to every chord of the fill
turn K3 1
tapkey b0
wait 200
expect prgplay 1
expect prgslot0 2
expect prgslot1 5
expect prgslot2 1
expect prgslot3 1
expect prgslot4 0
expect prgbars0 8
expect prgbars3 8
tapkey b4
wait 200
expect prgslot0 1
expect prgslot1 4
expect prgslot2 7
expect prgslot3 3
expect prgslot4 6
expect prgslot5 2
expect prgslot6 5
expect prgslot7 1
shot circle_whole.png
# it plays round: slot 1 is I (A), slot 2 IV (D), slot 3 vii (G)
tap PLAY
wait 3000
expect progpos 0
expect chordroot 9
tap EDIT
wait 1500
expect progpos 1
expect chordroot 2
tap EDIT
wait 1500
expect progpos 2
expect chordroot 7
# THEORY on it: the arrow on to iii (C)
tap HOME
wait 100
tap HOME
wait 100
expect view 37
spin SELECT -1
wait 300
spin SELECT -1
wait 1200
expect viz 8
shot circle_theory.png
# stored with the piece: SAVE, power off and on
tap HOME
wait 300
tap GLO
tap SAVE
wait 400
reboot
wait 3000
expect prgslot2 7
expect prgslot7 1
# a pentatonic (the mode on ALGORITHM, Pent min): no circle, nothing changed
setpar 72 7
wait 200
press EDIT
wait 600
release EDIT
wait 100
tapkey b0
wait 200
expect prgslot0 1
expect prgslot2 7
